{
  "id": "2026-09-17-table-substrate-ownership",
  "scope": "table",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-17",
  "question": "What owns table topology, cell coordinates, selection, clipboard and layout?",
  "model": "GPT-6 (exact runtime variant unavailable)",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2 + plite-research; first-principles cross-layer comparison",
  "trigger": "User explicitly requests deep first-principles table redesign and promotion assessment across Plite/Plate, especially selection and resizing, using external editor source research.",
  "requirements": [
    "One canonical document/change/selection authority with root identity, direction, mapping and history.",
    "Rich nested cell content, spans and complete slices; no second selected-cell store.",
    "Logical table actions available independently of React; browser geometry and gestures tied to the exact mounted view.",
    "Resize preview remains view-local; durable dimensions commit through canonical feature updates; cancellation discards preview.",
    "Host replacement must preserve selected attributes and retire old paint; runtime replacements need complete-operation behavior and scale proof.",
    "Review and research artifacts only; no product implementation, downstream plan or publication."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Re-read current table owners, Plite selection/mapping/host contracts, copied UI and prior design/closure. Retained prior content/target/mutation receipts and rejected React-paint benchmark as scoped historical evidence. Reconciled existing research leads. Four independent bounded investigations supplied upstream source evidence and an actual-hook local diagnostic. Seven upstream repositories are pinned; decisive stale snapshots received current-source supplements. No upstream tests were run. The fresh Happy DOM counterexample contradicts blanket verified paint coverage; it does not negate the earlier passing behaviors.",
  "summary": "Pursue headless Plate table selection and consolidated mounted interaction. Cut caller range assembly and copied gesture policy; compare shared active-boundary controls and deletion of the dedicated paint cache. Reproduced same-key DOM host replacement losing selected attributes/caret style. Keep topology, table width policy and canonical edits with their current feature/core owners; no blanket Plite table or public resize protocol.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-17-table-canonical-api-closure",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure: rejected; configuration cannot supply semantic selection commands or repair stale DOM hosts.",
    "Change existing API: pursue root-aware, inferred headless selection commands and logical navigation in the existing table owner.",
    "New core selection protocol: defer pending an unmet enduring-intent law; PM and Lexical are precedents, CKEditor demonstrates ordinary model-range composition.",
    "Strongest cut: remove UI range assembly and copied gesture policy; compare deleting permanent per-cell resize controls and the dedicated selection paint cache. Runtime implementations remain provisional pending direct proof and scale.",
    "Reuse existing rendered-attribute producer: compare efficient host binding with a narrow hook repair. Do not repeat the already-rejected React cell-render fan-out implementation.",
    "Move ownership: retain grid/span/clipboard/width policy in Plate, canonical selection/mapping/transactions in Plite, exact-view input in Plate React and appearance in copied UI. Promote a neutral host-lifetime primitive only if existing owners cannot express a proven job.",
    "Replace architecture: reject a new table substrate package, spreadsheet AST, parallel selection store, public controller/grid protocol, and universal box/table resizer. Existing rich-content and private planning jobs survive."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Source and test assertions inspected across seven repositories; exact snapshots and bounded current-head supplements are recorded. Existing paint-hook spec passed; fresh actual-hook Happy DOM probe passed 11 controls then failed selected attribute/caret style after same-key td-to-th replacement. No full production renderer/browser pixels, native caret, upstream test execution, physical devices or candidate performance claim. Prior paint benchmark rejects the naive React attribute candidate; alternative binding/shared-controls remain unmeasured. Prior adopted implementation remains adopted; current proof is partial because of the reproduced gap. Prior broad typecheck TS6307 limit and other historical receipts remain scoped to their recorded source. No product code, implementation plan, publication or release.",
